# WHY THE RECALL NUMBER IS NOT YET TRUSTWORTHY, AND WHAT WOULD FIX IT.
#
# Job 110 produced the project's first recall figure -- 0.174 overall, 0.243 in
# the 1-2 m band where the carrots land. Then the overlays were looked at, and
# they say the number is a floor, not a measurement:
#
#   frame 0    the magenta ground truth sits ON the painted line. Odom is zero
#              there, so the pose is exactly the spawn: the spawn fix and the
#              texture fix both landed.
#   frame 330  the magenta runs parallel to the paint but roughly half a metre
#              off, converging at the horizon and separating toward the camera
#              -- the signature of a lateral pose error, not a bad projection.
#   frames 480, 540, 600, 660 are BYTE-IDENTICAL. The robot wedged for the last
#              third of the capture, so 216 of the 672 frames are one frozen
#              pose repeated, and they all score against whatever that one view
#              contained.
#
# Aligned at the start, drifted by the middle: that is accumulating wheel
# odometry, and this run stalled repeatedly. Ignition's DiffDrive integrates
# joint motion, so a robot whose wheels turn while it does not move banks
# phantom distance. Misaligned labels can only push recall DOWN -- a prediction
# that lands on real paint scores as a false positive when the label is 0.5 m
# away -- so the true recall is higher than 0.174 by an unknown margin. The
# honest statement today is that we do not have a trustworthy recall number
# yet; we have a floor, and a named reason.
#
# THIS JOB DOES TWO SMALL THINGS, NO LAP RUNS, A FEW MINUTES.
#
# 1. Rescores the existing dataset with --dedup, and reports a statistic that
#    needs no ground truth at all: in how many frames the model predicted ANY
#    lane pixels. That separates "the model is blind at this camera" from "the
#    labels are in the wrong place" -- and it is the one number today's data
#    can support honestly.
#
# 2. Finds out whether Gazebo already publishes a ground-truth pose we can
#    bridge. If it does, capture_labelled.py should use it instead of /odom and
#    the drift disappears at the source. This PROBES rather than patches: the
#    bridge list is guesswork from here, and this project has already spent a
#    night on a confidently wrong guess about /dev/shm.
set -uo pipefail
cd "$ESDA_HOME"
source esda_lib.sh
bash setup_wsl.sh --sync > /tmp/sync110b.log 2>&1 || { tail -20 /tmp/sync110b.log; exit 1; }

echo "=== 1. rescore, de-duplicated, with the alignment-free statistic ==="
DS="$(ls -1dt "$HOME"/esda_datasets/rescore_* 2>/dev/null | head -1)"
[ -n "$DS" ] || { echo "no rescore dataset -- run 110 first"; exit 1; }
echo "dataset: $DS"
python3 vision/eval_recall.py --data "$DS" --split val --dedup \
        --weights "$HOME/esda_models/lane_seg.pt" --conf 0.35 \
        2>&1 | tee "$ESDA_HOME/logs/eval_recall_dedup.txt"

echo
echo "=== 2. is there a ground-truth pose to bridge? ==="
bash demo.sh up --no-rviz --world igvc_oval_slow_test >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
sleep 5

echo "--- gz topics mentioning pose ---"
( ign topic -l 2>/dev/null || gz topic -l 2>/dev/null ) | grep -iE "pose|odom" | sed 's/^/   /'

echo "--- ROS topics mentioning pose or odom ---"
ros2 topic list 2>/dev/null | grep -iE "pose|odom|tf" | sed 's/^/   /'

echo "--- what publishes /tf, and does it carry a world->base_link ---"
ros2 topic info /tf 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^/   /'
timeout 5 ros2 topic echo /tf --once 2>/dev/null | head -25 | sed 's/^/   /'

echo "--- one sample from each gz pose topic (names tell us which model) ---"
for t in $( ( ign topic -l 2>/dev/null || gz topic -l 2>/dev/null ) | grep -iE "pose" | head -4 ); do
  echo "   >> $t"
  ( timeout 4 ign topic -e -t "$t" 2>/dev/null || timeout 4 gz topic -e -t "$t" 2>/dev/null ) \
    | head -20 | sed 's/^/      /'
done

echo "--- /odom one sample, for comparison ---"
timeout 5 ros2 topic echo /odom --once 2>/dev/null | head -18 | sed 's/^/   /'

stop_all >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
echo
echo "READ: if a gz topic carries the robot model's world pose, bridge it and"
echo "point capture_labelled.py at it with a --pose-topic flag. Ground truth in"
echo "a simulator should never be integrated from wheels; it is sitting right"
echo "there in the physics engine. Then recapture (short, and check it did not"
echo "wedge) and the recall number becomes one we can quote."
